{title: Sing Praise to God Who Reigns Above}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Sing [C]praise to God who [F]reigns a[C]bove; The [Dm]God of [G]all cre[**]a[C]tion
The [C]God of pow'r, the [F]God of [C]love; The [Dm]God of [G]our sal[**]va[C]tion
With [Em]healing balm [Am]my [D]soul is [G]filled
And [C]ev'ry faithless [D]murmur [G]stilled
To [F]God all [G]praise and [**]glo[C]ry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C]Lord is never [F]far a[C]way [A]But [Dm]thro' all [G]grief dis[**]tress-[C]ing
An [C]ever present [F]help and [C]stay; our [Dm]peace and [G]joy and [**]bless[C]ing
As [Em]with a moth[Am]er's [D]tender [G]hand
God [C]gently leads the [D]chosen [G]band
To [F]God all [G]praise and [**]glo[C]ry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Thus [C]all my toilsome [F]way a[C]long; I [Dm]sing a[G]loud Thy [**]prais[C]es
That [C]earth may hear the [F]grateful [C]song; my [Dm]voice un[G]wearied [**]rais[C]es
Be [Em]joyful in [Am]the [D]Lord, my [G]heart
